   "evidence": "`def helicityChanges (twoJ : \u2115) : Set \u2124 := {d | \u2203 m m', m.natAbs \u2264 twoJ \u2227 m'.natAbs \u2264 twoJ \u2227 ... \u2227 2 * d = m - m'}` (Transversity.lean:63) quantifies only over target sublevels; the roadmap spec says \"The statement is deliberately about the target's representation rather than about the gluon operator\" (roadmap/EpsilonEridaniRoadmaps/SpinStructure/Suggested.lean:241-243).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/Transversity.lean",
   "fix": "Drop \"of an operator `O` carrying angular momentum `J`\": say the set records the helicity changes `d = (m - m')/2` between two states of the target, which bounds any operator's contribution to a forward matrix element.",
   "issue": "The module doc states \"A forward matrix element `\u27e8m'| O |m\u27e9` of an operator `O` carrying angular momentum `J` can only connect states whose helicity change ... is recorded in `helicityChanges twoJ`\". `helicityChanges` has no dependence on the operator or its rank \u2014 it is a statement about the target representation only (`J` here is the target spin, so the clause additionally reads as an unrelated and false constraint tying the operator's rank to the target spin).",
   "line": 42
  }
